# Paths Opengrep skips. gitignore syntax, read from the scan root. Generated
# trees are never hand-edited (so a finding there is not actionable), and test
# code is out of the SAST scope — its "unsafe" patterns are fixtures and helpers,
# not shipped behavior.

# --- the rule tree itself (config, not scanned source) ---
.semgrep/

# --- generated code (regenerated from a source; never edited) ---
gen/
generated/
**/*.pb.go
**/*_pb2*.py
**/*_pb2.pyi
**/mocks/

# --- vendored / build / tooling output ---
node_modules/
dist/
.venv/

# --- docs (prose, not code) ---
docs/

# --- tests (fixtures and helpers, not shipped behavior) ---
**/tests/**
*_test.go
